cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, cite it with the metadata below. Cite the underlying data through the references in docs/data/manifest.qmd."
title: "gia-mip: case definitions and reference data for GIA benchmarks and GIAMIP"
type: software
version: 0.1.0.dev0
date-released: 2026-09-11
repository-code: "https://github.com/g-adopt/gia-mip"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Machine-readable case definitions, converted reference data and output
  conventions for two published glacial isostatic adjustment benchmarks (Spada
  et al. 2011 and Martinec et al. 2018) and for the Glacial Isostatic Adjustment
  Model Intercomparison Project. The repository specifies what to run and holds
  what to compare against. It contains no solver.
authors:
  - family-names: Ghelichkhan
    given-names: Siavash
    affiliation: Australian National University
